# screenshot.schema — which layer may decide each key of the `screenshot` subsystem.
#
# Read by /usr/lib/w/w-conf-lib.sh (and its Python twin) during the load
# pass; a user-layer assignment to a `system` key is dropped with a warning, and
# `wconf_set` refuses to write it in the first place. See w-conf.md.
#
# Format: <KEY>\t<scope>       scope: system | user | both
#   system — root domain: the admin (or fleet policy) decides, per machine.
#   user   — the logged-in user may override it in ~/.config/w/screenshot.conf.
#   both   — either layer may speak; the usual priority order applies.
#
# The only key here is `user`: which annotation UI opens is a matter of personal
# taste inside one graphical session, it touches nothing outside that user's own
# screen, and both tools are installed on every machine anyway. A fleet that
# wants to pin one of them still can — policy.d sits above the user layer.

ANNOTATOR	user
